 {:db/id -14 :cell/plane "kotobase" :cell/stride "elevation-of-privilege"
  :cell/linddun "non-compliance" :cell/status :implemented :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
  :cell/surface "kotobase authorize-xrpc"
  :cell/evidence "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase src/kotobase/kotobase.cljc + test/kotobase/authorize_xrpc_test.cljc, pin c722fb166b11"
  :cell/finding "ADR-2607280100 Step 3: the lattice is evaluated on reads, not only writes. Egress stays a write question; every method now emits a classification-decision labelled read or write. abac's required-rank is nil for an undeclared resource and nil raises no violation, so unclassified read as allowed for the same reason cleared ones do -- the decision records which happened, and classification-required? turns the first into :kotobase/classification-undeclared. The comparison stays in abac (D6); this layer only records whether abac was given enough to make it."
  :cell/had-no-tests-before true
  :cell/gap "opt-in: a caller that omits classification-required? is unchanged. Making declaration unconditional is Step 4's compile-time job."}

 {:db/id -13 :cell/plane "kotobase" :cell/stride "elevation-of-privilege"
  :cell/linddun "data-disclosure" :cell/status :implemented :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
  :cell/surface "kotobase-peer read policy"
  :cell/evidence "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer src/kotobase_peer/policy.cljc, pin ed3ae49d79ec"
  :cell/finding "ADR-2607280100 Step 2 (D3) landed: read visibility is four-level, (>= viewer-rank level-rank), over the one lattice in kotoba-lang/security rather than a local copy. A prefix with no declared level is :restricted, so the previous binary rule is the top case of the new one -- breaking the object-side rounding fails the PRE-EXISTING tests, which is the evidence for that. Unknown labels round UP on the object side and DOWN on the subject side; a shared rule would be wrong on one of them."
  :cell/first-implementation-in-this-plane true
  :cell/gap "nothing mints read-classified/<label> capabilities yet -- four levels can be declared and enforced, not handed out"}

 {:db/id -5 :cell/plane "kotobase" :cell/stride "information-disclosure"
  :cell/linddun "data-disclosure" :cell/status :measured :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
  :cell/evidence "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase docs/disclosure-surface-measurement.md"
  :cell/finding "A receipt cannot carry an identity. receipt-keys is exactly nine fields, exact-keys! refuses :principal as :invalid-keys, and forbidden-keys walks nested values so a credential under :cost is :forbidden-field. :principal lives in the request envelope, cited only by digest."}

 {:db/id -6 :cell/plane "kotobase" :cell/stride "information-disclosure"
  :cell/linddun "linking" :cell/status :measured :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
  :cell/evidence "orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase docs/disclosure-surface-measurement.md"
  :cell/finding "The envelope nonce reaches :request/digest, the receipt, and the receipt's own address, so two runs of the same query by the same principal share no public identifier and the transparency leaf does not repeat."}

