 {:db/id -9 :cell/plane "agent" :cell/stride "elevation-of-privilege"
  :cell/linddun "non-compliance" :cell/status :gap :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
  :cell/evidence "orgs/kotoba-lang/ayatori src/ayatori/agent.cljc"
  :cell/finding "Measured 2026-09-10 by running it. validate refuses 22 of 30 probes across 11 literals and allows 8; blinding the unknown-attribute branch flips 7 to allowed, blinding entity-position flips 2, and blinding the :where walk flips 25 to :unbound-find-var rather than to allowed, so that check is a backstop. 0 of the 11 literals mention authority, permission, visibility, principal or tenant, and neither does the arity: a third argument naming a principal is accepted and silently discarded while the query stays allowed, where omitting the schema fails closed. A validated query does reach execution with nothing between: the same query reading a sensitive attribute returns 2 rows under the visible? the workspace query adapter actually passes -- manifest/edn_query_datalog.cljs line 112, (constantly true), the single such call site outside docstrings -- and 0 rows under a visible? that denies it, so the seam works and the adapter holds it open. Of 17 files referencing the namespace, 2 are real non-test consumers, both benchmarks, and 0 of 2 perform an authority check between validation and execution. Stages 4 through 7 of the stated pipeline have no code in this tree: there is nothing to enforce because nothing was written."
  :cell/evidence-harness "orgs/kotoba-lang/ayatori scripts/measure-agent-validate.cljs + scripts/measure-agent-execution-reach.cljs, pin d6f343139c69"
  :cell/not-measured "no model was called: whether an LLM in practice writes queries that pass validate and read what it should not is unmeasured; only that nothing would stop it"}

 {:db/id -10 :cell/plane "kotoba" :cell/stride "tampering"
  :cell/linddun "non-compliance" :cell/status :gap :source/dataset "privacy-plane"
